From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Heimbrock <43608204+MaxHeimbrock@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:17:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix: render external custom types locally and inherit
 their config

Upstream: https://github.com/NordSecurity/uniffi-bindgen-cs/pull/185 (open), cherry-picked.
Needed for AnilistId, ProviderKey and JobId, custom types of one crate used by another.

Custom types are rendered as file-scoped C# `using` aliases, but
ExternalTypeTemplate.cs treated a custom type from another crate like a
record: it referenced the other file's alias as a type (CS0246) and its
alias as a converter class (CS0234).

Route external custom types through CustomTypeTemplate.cs so the
consuming file declares its own aliases, or its own converter class when
the type is configured. Drop the unreachable `is_external` branch in the
local-types loop; iter_local_types() never yields external types.

Because every file renders the type itself, copy `custom_types` entries
from the defining crate into each crate that uses the type, unless that
crate configures it itself, the same way external_packages is filled in.

Add two custom types to the ext-types base fixture (one unconfigured, one
mapped to System.Uri via a new uniffi.toml), consumer functions using them
directly and inside Option, Vec and a record, and a new test class.
Existing fixtures and tests are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Max Heimbrock <43608204+MaxHeimbrock@users.noreply.github.com>
